@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+# Lighter Desert road and Grass-sand tire tracks
+
+Owner request, 2026-10-14: use the tire-track treatment seen on sand in the Grass biome, lighten the Desert road slightly, and match the marks to that road colour.
+
+Requirements: DST01 shared sand tread/groove/opacity; DST02 modest road lightening with continuous bridge mouths; DST03 matching road/mark pigment; V05 retained bounded rendering and first-use preparation; G01/R01 retained canonical driving, dust and replay; Q01 actual evidence and limitations.
+
+The road pigment changes from `9f8052` to `ac8b5a`. Only `TrackTheme.DESERT[0]` changes; shoulders, dunes, artwork, sun, lighting and camera retain their existing values. Ground roads and native/creator bridge decks already share this palette. The visual kit advances from 198 to 199 to fence prepared geometry that includes bound palette materials.
+
+Desert tracks retain the shared four-vertex/two-triangle ribbon and now use the same tread/centre/shoulder contrast and analytic groove normal as Grass-biome sand. The Desert-only flat-normal, softened-tread and additional high-pressure darkening overrides are removed. Maximum opacity changes from 0.24 to the shared sand value of 0.52. The matte Desert specular treatment remains. A `source_color` uniform binds the exact road pigment, without the previous 0.92 RGB multiplier. Shaded grooves naturally have different light values from the flat road while sharing its base pigment.
+
+No new textures, geometry, draws or samplers are introduced by this change. Width, relief, endpoint joins, pressure interpolation, four-wheel contact/intensity sampling, 0.32 m spacing, the 16,384-slot ring, bridge clipping and covered first draw are retained. This task does not edit dust, canonical physics, handling, content contracts, scoring, replay or camera code.
+
+Changed files: `game/vehicle/skid_trails.gd`, `game/track/track_theme.gd`, `game/track/native_track_visual.gd`; review-only extensions to `game/tests/capture_desert_tire_marks.gd` and an optional output folder in `game/tests/test_trail_render_preparation.gd`; this report, `AGENTS.md`, `DEVELOPMENT_STATUS.md` and `docs/PHASE_0_PLAN.md`. Build identity/project version files are regenerated by the existing launcher and excluded from the task checkpoint.
+
+The capture's optional `--extended` records cornering and five slightly displaced overlapping braking passes. `--baseline` loads the saved entry tire renderer and rebinds the old road pigment in the frozen native scene; it does not swap live workspace source files. The baseline tire renderer uses the live car's exact wheelbase/track width. The diagnostic clears the automatic pause overlay before every saved frame. All captures use detached presentation state and preserve the actual canonical state snapshot, cells and content hash; these are cosmetic samples, not completed races or player telemetry. Dust is deliberately absent from the frozen comparison.
+
+Actual commands use pinned Godot `4.7.2.stable.official.ed1daf0bf` through `scripts/dev.ps1`. Process-local APPDATA/LOCALAPPDATA are isolated under `build/desert_sand_tracks_2026_10_14/user-data`; native execution was approved for Windows certificate-store access. `-RenderingMethod gl_compatibility` and `-RenderingMethod mobile -RenderingDriver vulkan` select the two desktop renderers. `TestArgument` contains the task evidence folder and, where listed, `--extended` or `--baseline`.
+
+| Actual action | Outcome |
+| --- | --- |
+| `TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/capture_desert_tire_marks.gd -Graphical` on both renderers | Final rolling/braking/loose-sand images and surface controls; 396 segments each. Entry alpha 0.0647/0.1045 becomes 0.1402/0.2264. Canonical snapshot/cells/hash preserved. |
+| Same with `--extended`, both renderers | Ten views each, including cornering (396 segments) and five overlapping passes (1,980 segments), with matching surface controls. Same canonical checks pass. |
+| Same with `--baseline --extended`, Mobile/Vulkan | Ten unobstructed saved-source control views, correct original pigment/alpha, exact canonical checks. Supersedes the initial paused Mobile control. |
+| `TestSoil` | 163 checks, zero failures. |
+| `TestDesert` | 87 checks, zero failures; original dust and all five cars' packed/loose-sand replay behavior. |
+| `TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_tire_ribbons.gd` | 14 checks, zero failures; joins, immutable endpoints, pressure, resets and ring/geometry budget. Its historical geometry-control timing is not a performance comparison for this material change. |
+| `TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_desert_bank_bridge_blend.gd -Graphical`, both renderers | 656 + 656 checks, zero failures. Actual UV/apron/sampler/canonical checks and bridge seam pixels. Maximum entry/exit RGB deltas: Compatibility 0.029607/0.019996; Mobile 0.031859/0.019608, within the unchanged 0.035 threshold. |
+| `TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_bridge_trails.gd -Graphical`, both renderers | 8 + 8 checks, zero failures. Unprotected roof contamination 9,810/9,747 pixels becomes zero with the retained guard; legitimate deck marks and independent ground/deck layers remain. |
+| `TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_trail_render_preparation.gd -Graphical`, Compatibility | 38 checks, zero failures, clean exit. Actual covered draw shares the live mesh/Shader RID and restores exact ring/material/history/pixels/camera/condition/countdown. Normal launch keeps one tire batch and no fabricated marks. |
+| Same, Mobile/Vulkan | Final rerun: 38 checks, zero failures and clean exit, with the same exact restoration checks. Initial run printed all 38 passing assertions, then timed out during engine shutdown after 300 seconds; that initial launcher result remains a failure. |
+| `TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_script_parse.gd` | 742 scripts, zero failures at that checkpoint. Subsequent capture-fixture additions compile and run in native Mobile captures. |
+| Source preservation / scoped whitespace | Eleven trail functions remain exact relative to the merged task control, including sampling, bridge clipping, intensity, width, relief, joins and mesh. Other styles and lighting/palettes remain exact within this task's scope. Scoped source proof is in `preserved-source.json`. |
+
+Final road-only image sampling uses 5,400 identical positions inside a clear central road region, with the same camera and no marks. Mean display-weighted RGB luma rises 7.45% in Compatibility and 5.43% in Mobile. These figures describe this screenshot region, not material linear luminance, performance or every scene. `road-pixels.json` records coordinates and source folders. The initial paused Mobile calculation is retained as invalid evidence in `road-pixels-initial-paused.json` and is not used for the final claim.
+
+Inspect [Compatibility braking](evidence/desert-sand-tracks-2026-10-14/extended-compatibility/braking.png), [Mobile braking](evidence/desert-sand-tracks-2026-10-14/extended-mobile/braking.png), [five-pass overlap](evidence/desert-sand-tracks-2026-10-14/extended-compatibility/overlapping.png), and the [Mobile original road control](evidence/desert-sand-tracks-2026-10-14/control-mobile/rolling-surface.png). These and the rolling/cornering/surface controls were visually reviewed.
+
+Concurrent road-mud pigment/fade/encoding work appeared in the same `skid_trails.gd` during this task. It is preserved and excluded from the Desert checkpoint by reversing only this task's Desert edits into a merged control. Original entry snapshots remain separate. The initial strict whole-file preservation probe correctly detected that concurrent `_mark` change; it was not bypassed or attributed to this task. No broad claim of byte-exact other-biome pixels across concurrent tasks is made.
+
+Initial ordinary launches failed on sandbox user-log and Windows certificate-store access; isolated test data and approved native execution resolved those startup restrictions. Initial Mobile baseline images contain the automatic pause overlay and are superseded by `control-mobile`. Frozen bridge diagnostics print large frame intervals while doing screenshot/pixel-analysis work; they are not phone or live race pacing measurements.
+
+Reviewable task-only Git checkpoint: `build/desert_sand_tracks_2026_10_14/checkpoint-repo`; patch and receipt in `docs/evidence/desert-sand-tracks-2026-10-14/`. The main Git index and unrelated changes are preserved. No physical-phone test, Android export/install, backend operation, deployment or full physics merge was performed; device attachment was not checked. Owner review of the final road shade/grooves and physical-phone appearance/performance remain acceptance checks. No FPS or general hitch-free claim is made.
